# Course Module Markdown

Conversational lesson content as `.md` files inside **module folders** (for example `Module 02 - Search, Sort, and Interactive Structure/content.md`).

This repo follows the same conventions as [C++Book](../C++Book/.cursor/rules/textbook-md-chapters.mdc). When in doubt, match that style.

## Structure

| Term | Meaning | Example |
|------|---------|---------|
| **Module** | A topic folder and its lesson files | `Module 02 - Search, Sort, and Interactive Structure/` |
| **Content file** | The main lesson `.md` in a module folder | `content.md` |

Inside a content file, `##` / `###` headings are **blocks** within that lesson, not separate modules.

## Voice

- One concept at a time; build on earlier modules when needed.
- Plain language, short paragraphs; explain **why**, not only **what**.
- End sections with something to **try** when hands-on practice fits.
- Do not use em dashes (`—`), en dashes as punctuation (`–`), or `--` as a stand-in. Use a period, comma, colon, parentheses, or split into two sentences instead.

## Headings

| Level | Use |
|-------|-----|
| `#` | Lesson title, **once** at the top |
| `##` | Major blocks (hook, core concept, examples, mistakes, summary) |
| `###` | Subsections within a `##` block |

## Callouts

Every line of a callout must start with `>`. Use exactly one prefix: `NOTE:`, `PREFERENCE:`, `PROTIP:`, `HISTORY:`, `AI:`.

## Code and examples

- Use `cpp` for runnable C++ examples.
- Use `sdl2` for interactive SDL2 demos (640×480 canvas in TxtBook).
- Do not use `using namespace std;` in C++ examples.
- Prefer `.at()` instead of `[]` for container access.
- Prefer zero-based `for` loops when the variable only counts iterations.
- Use vertically aligned braces in normal C++ examples.
- Put `int main()` before helper function **definitions** in single-file examples.
- One `cpp` fence per playground; use `// @file:` for multi-file examples.
- For SDL2: `#include <SDL2/SDL.h>`, call `SDL_Delay(16)` once per frame, load assets once before the loop.

See C++Book rules for full TxtBook playground, SDL2 asset, and details-block conventions.
